  "worked_solution": "Here, we let $u(x)=arccotx$ and $v(x)={x}^{3},$ and apply the quotient rule.\n\nWe use the formulae\n\n$$\n{u}^{\u2032}(x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{and}\\,{v}^{\u2032}(x)=3{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{u}^{\u2032}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{\u2032}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\cdot {x}^{3}-arccotx\\cdot 3{x}^{2}}{({x}^{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{1+{x}^{2}}-3{x}^{2}arccotx}{{x}^{6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{(\\frac{{x}^{3}+3(1+{x}^{2}){x}^{2}arccotx}{1+{x}^{2}})}{{x}^{6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{x}^{3}+3(1+{x}^{2}){x}^{2}arccotx}{{x}^{6}(1+{x}^{2})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{x+3(1+{x}^{2})arccotx}{{x}^{4}(1+{x}^{2})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
